$DATUM 919-30-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):AMD
$DATUM surface reaction products with SBA-15
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Rhodanines (3a-3g) and 2,4-Thiazolidinediones (3h-3n) . A mixture of the
aromatic aldehyde (1 mmol), 2,4-thiazolidinedione (0.133, 1 mmol) [or
rhoda-nine (0.117 g, 1 mmol)] and SBA-15-Pr-NH2 (0.05 g) in EtOH (5 mL)
was stirred at 50°C in an oil bath for 2 hours; the progress of the
reaction was monitored by TLC (2:1 n-hexane/ethyl acetate). After
completion of the reaction, 10 mL acetone was added and the mixture was
filtered to remove the catalyst. Upon addition of 5 mL H2O to the
filtrate, the precipitated solid obtained was collected and
recrystallized from ethanol. The pure products, characterized by
comparison of their 1H NMR spectra and melting points with those reported
in the literature. Compound: 3f; Yield: 95%. Mp: Found: 225-227°C; Lit.:
224-2304 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, solid-supported catalyst, catalyst prepared and
used, recyclable catalyst, silica support used, Knoevenagel condensation,
optimization study, optimized on reaction conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 5-Alkylidene-2,4-thiazolidinediones and Rhodanines Promoted
