$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
(Z)-5-((3-aryl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-diones
(3a–h) A mixture of 1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-carboxaldehyde (1a, 1g, 4
mmol) and thiazolidine-2,4-dione (2, 0.51 g, 5 mmol) in ethanol (20 ml)
and 2–3 drops of piperidine, was refluxed. A solid separated out of the
reaction mixture within 15–20 min and the refluxing was continued for 5–6
h to complete the reaction. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, filtered and washed with ethanol to give the pure product.
(Z)-5-((3-(4-bromophenyl)-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-dione
(3f), 93% IR cm-1 (KBr): 1751 (C=O, thiazolidinedione ring), 1690 (C=O,
thiazolidinedione ring), 1597, 1528, 1497, 1450, 1412, 1335, 1227, 1142,
1088, 1057 and 1011; 1H NMR δ (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): 12.5–12.7 (bs, 1H, NH,
exch. D2O), 8.703 (s, 1H, Pyrazolyl-H), 8.019–7.993 (d, 2H, J = 7.8 Hz),
7.656–7.647 (m, 4H), 7.588–7.543 (m, 3H), 7.443–7.396 (m, 1H). 13C NMR δ
(75 MHz, DMSO-d6): 167.97, 167.56, 152.69, 139.16, 134.37, 130.81,
130.10, 129.52, 128.69, 128.04, 123.62, 122.14, 119.88 and 116.04. Anal.
Found: C, 53.45; H, 2.96; N, 9.77. C19H12BrN3O2S (426.29) requires C,
53.53; H, 2.84; N, 9.86%. Mp = 301–303 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Knoevenagel condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and antimicrobial activity of
5-((3-aryl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-diones
