$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.11. Preparation of methyl
2-((Z)-5-((3-aryl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)-2,4-dioxothiazolidin-3-yl)acetates
(5a-h) Typical procedure: A mixture of
1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-carboxaldehyde 1a (0.5 g, 2 mmol) and methyl
2-(2,4-dioxothiazolidin-3-yl)acetate 2 (0.38 g, 2 mmol) in methanol (20
ml) and 2-3 drops of piperidine was refluxed 4-5 h. A solid was separated
out of the reaction mixture within 15-20 min and the refluxing was
continued for 4-5 h to complete the reaction. The reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature, filtered and washed with methanol to give the
pure product 5a. The other derivatives 5b-h were synthesized by adopting
the similar procedure. Methyl
2-((Z)-5-((3-(4-nitrophenyl)-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)-2,4-dioxothiazolidin-3-yl)acetate
(5h), yield 93%. IR (νmax, KBr) cm-1: 1744, 1690, 1605, 1528, 1412, 1342,
1273, 1219, 1142, 1103. 1H NMR (CDCl3 + TFA-d1, 400 MHz, δ): 8.454-8.434
(d, 2H, Ar H, J= 8.8 Hz), 8.261-8.247 (m, 2H, Ar H), 7.906-7.834 (m, 3H,
Ar H), 7.710-7.689 (m, 2H, Ar H), 7.637-7.571 (m, 2H, Ar H), 4.642 (s,
2H, NCH2), 3.985 (s, 3H, COOCH3). MS (ESI+) m/z 450 [M+H]. Anal. Found:
C, 58.7; H, 3.6; N, 11.8. C22H16N4O6S requires C, 58.89; H, 3.47; N,
12.06%. Melting points (°C): 240-242.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Knoevenagel condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
